import Wikipedia.HopfProblem.TrianglePeriodFamilyGammaZeroTorus
import Wikipedia.HopfProblem.TrianglePeriodFamilyGammaZeroSpecial

/-!
# The native zero-γ regular torus subfamily and actual `H₄` detection

The original triangle representation preserves the first real torus
coordinate.  Its zero fibre in the actual regular quotient family has
genuine three-torus fibres.  Restricting the original slit charts gives
the real product charts and a continuous retraction on the whole slit
overlap.  The actual singular Mayer--Vietoris sequence then proves that
the original source-kernel projection is injective on the fourth-homology
image of this subfamily.

The special-period version has no additional geometric inputs.  This
package does not identify an attachment matrix or assert injectivity
for the full global attachment map.
-/
